**1. Conditional Test Logic** (testsmells.org: *Conditional Test Logic*)
- **Method:** `ProcessOrder_SetsCorrectStatus` (line 24)
- **Evidence:** `if (result.TotalAmount > 100) ... else ...` on lines 31–38 gates which assertion runs.
- **Risk:** One branch is never exercised per run — half the test is dead code.
- **Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_StandardOrder_SetsStandardStatus()
{
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-1", 2) } };
    var result = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory).ProcessOrder(order);
    Assert.AreEqual("StandardProcessed", result.Status);
}

[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_PremiumOrder_SetsPremiumStatus()
{
    // Use items whose total > 100
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-EXPENSIVE", 5) } };
    var result = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory).ProcessOrder(order);
    Assert.AreEqual("PremiumProcessed", result.Status);
}
```

